le overrides the artifact name. Packaging -&gt; (string) Only used when Type is S3 . The type of output artifact to create. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Path -&gt; (string) Only used when Type is S3 . The path to the artifact. Used with Name and Name- spaceType to determine the pattern for storing the artifact. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Type -&gt; (string) The type of build artifact. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsCloudFrontDistribution -&gt; (structure) Details about a CloudFront distribution. CacheBehaviors -&gt; (structure) Provides information about the cache configura- tion for the distribution. Items -&gt; (list) The cache behaviors for the distribution. (structure) Information about a cache behavior for the distribution. ViewerProtocolPolicy -&gt; (string) The protocol that viewers can use to access the files in an origin. You can specify the following options: o allow-all - Viewers can use HTTP or HTTPS. o redirect-to-https - CloudFront re- sponds to HTTP requests with an HTTP status code of 301 (Moved Permanently) and the HTTPS URL. The viewer then uses the new URL to resubmit. o https-only - CloudFront responds to HTTP request with an HTTP sta- tus code of 403 (Forbidden). Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DefaultCacheBehavior -&gt; (structure) The default cache behavior for the configura- tion. ViewerProtocolPolicy -&gt; (string) The protocol that viewers can use to access the files in an origin. You can specify the following options: o allow-all - Viewers can use HTTP or HTTPS. o redirect-to-https - CloudFront responds to HTTP requests with an HTTP status code of 301 (Moved Permanently) and the HTTPS URL. The viewer then uses the new URL to resubmit. o https-only - CloudFront responds to HTTP request with an HTTP status code of 403 (Forbidden). Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DefaultRootObject -&gt; (string) The object that CloudFront sends in response to requests from the origin (for example, in- dex.html) when a viewer requests the root URL for the distribution (http://www.example.com) instead of an object in your distribution (- http://www.example.com/product-descrip- tion.html). Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DomainName -&gt; (string) The domain name corresponding to the distribu- tion. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* ETag -&gt; (string) The entity tag is a hash of the object. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LastModifiedTime -&gt; (string) Indicates when that the distribution was last modified. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Logging -&gt; (structure) A complex type that controls whether access logs are written for the distribution. Bucket -&gt; (string) The S3 bucket to store the access logs in. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Enabled -&gt; (boolean) With this field, you can enable or disable the selected distribution. IncludeCookies -&gt; (boolean) Specifies whether you want CloudFront to include cookies in access logs. Prefix -&gt; (string) An optional string that you want CloudFront to use as a prefix to the access log file- names for this distribution. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Origins -&gt; (structure) A complex type that contains information about origins for this distribution. Items -&gt; (list) A complex type that contains origins or origin groups for this distribution. (structure) A complex type that describes the Amazon S3 bucket, HTTP server (for example, a web server), or other server from which CloudFront gets your files. DomainName -&gt; (string) Amazon S3 origins: The DNS name of the S3 bucket from which you want CloudFront to get objects for this origin. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Id -&gt; (string) A unique identifier for the origin or origin group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* OriginPath -&gt; (string) An optional element that causes CloudFront to request your content from a directory in your Amazon S3 bucket or your custom origin. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* S3OriginConfig -&gt; (structure) An origin that is an S3 bucket that is not configured with static web- site hosting. OriginAccessIdentity -&gt; (string) The CloudFront origin access identity to associate with the origin. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CustomOriginConfig -&gt; (structure) An origin that is not an Amazon S3 bucket, with one exception. If the Amazon S3 bucket is configured with static website hosting, use this at- tribute. If the Amazon S3 bucket is not configured with static website hosting, use the S3OriginConfig type instead. HttpPort -&gt; (integer) The HTTP port that CloudFront uses to connect to the origin. HttpsPort -&gt; (integer) The HTTPS port that CloudFront uses to connect to the origin. OriginKeepaliveTimeout -&gt; (integer) Specifies how long, in seconds, CloudFront persists its connec- tion to the origin. OriginProtocolPolicy -&gt; (string) Specifies the protocol (HTTP or HTTPS) that CloudFront uses to connect to the origin. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* OriginReadTimeout -&gt; (integer) Specifies how long, in seconds, CloudFront waits for a response from the origin. OriginSslProtocols -&gt; (structure) Specifies the minimum SSL/TLS protocol that CloudFront uses when connecting to your origin over HTTPS. Items -&gt; (list) A list that contains allowed SSL/TLS protocols for this distribution. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Quantity -&gt; (integer) The number of SSL/TLS proto- cols that you want to allow CloudFront to use when estab- lishing an HTTPS connection with this origin. OriginGroups -&gt; (structure) Provides information about the origin groups in the distribution. Items -&gt; (list) The list of origin groups. (structure) Information about an origin group for the CloudFront distribution. FailoverCriteria -&gt; (structure) Provides the criteria for an origin group to fail over. StatusCodes -&gt; (structure) Information about the status codes that cause an origin group to fail over. Items -&gt; (list) The list of status code val- ues that can cause a failover to the next origin. (integer) Quantity -&gt; (integer) The number of status codes that can cause a failover. ViewerCertificate -&gt; (structure) Provides information about the TLS/SSL configu- ration that the distribution uses to communi- cate with viewers. AcmCertificateArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the ACM certificate. Used if the certificate is stored in ACM. If you pro- vide an ACM certificate ARN, you must also provide MinimumCertificateVersion and SslSupportMethod . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Certificate -&gt; (string) The identifier of the certificate. Note that in CloudFront, this attribute is dep- recated. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CertificateSource -&gt; (string) The source of the certificate identified by Certificate . Note that in CloudFront, this attribute is deprecated. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CloudFrontDefaultCertificate -&gt; (boolean) Whether the distribution uses the Cloud- Front domain name. If set to false , then you provide either AcmCertificateArn or IamCertificateId . IamCertificateId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the IAM certificate. Used if the certificate is stored in IAM. If you provide IamCertificateId , then you also must provide MinimumProtocolVersion and SslSupportMethod . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* MinimumProtocolVersion -&gt; (string) The security policy that CloudFront uses for HTTPS connections with viewers. If SslSupportMethod is sni-only , then Mini- mumProtocolVersion must be TLSv1 or higher. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SslSupportMethod -&gt; (string) The viewers that the distribution accepts HTTPS connections from. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Status -&gt; (string) Indicates the current status of the distribu- tion. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* WebAclId -&gt; (string) A unique identifier that specifies the WAF web ACL, if any, to associate with this distribu- tion. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsEc2Instance -&gt; (structure) Details about an EC2 instance related to a find- ing. Type -&gt; (string) The instance type of the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* ImageId -&gt; (string) The Amazon Machine Image (AMI) ID of the in- stance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* IpV4Addresses -&gt; (list) The IPv4 addresses associated with the in- stance. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* IpV6Addresses -&gt; (list) The IPv6 addresses associated with the in- stance. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KeyName -&gt; (string) The key name associated with the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* IamInstanceProfileArn -&gt; (string) The IAM profile ARN of the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VpcId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the VPC that the instance was launched in. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SubnetId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the subnet that the instance was launched in. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LaunchedAt -&gt; (string) Indicates when the instance was launched. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* NetworkInterfaces -&gt; (list) The identifiers of the network interfaces for the EC2 instance. The details for each network interface are in a corresponding AwsEc2Network- InterfacesDetails object. (structure) Identifies a network interface for the Ama- zon EC2 instance. NetworkInterfaceId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the network interface. The details are in a corresponding AwsEc2NetworkInterfacesDetails object. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VirtualizationType -&gt; (string) The virtualization type of the Amazon Machine Image (AMI) required to launch the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* MetadataOptions -&gt; (structure) Details about the metadata options for the Ama- zon EC2 instance. HttpEndpoint -&gt; (string) Enables or disables the HTTP metadata end- point on the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* HttpProtocolIpv6 -&gt; (string) Enables or disables the IPv6 endpoint for the instance metadata service. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* HttpPutResponseHopLimit -&gt; (integer) The desired HTTP PUT response hop limit for instance metadata requests. The larger the number, the further instance metadata re- quests can travel. HttpTokens -&gt; (string) The state of token usage for your instance metadata requests. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* InstanceMetadataTags -&gt; (string) Specifies whether to allow access to in- stance tags from the instance metadata. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Monitoring -&gt; (structure) Describes the type of monitoring thats turned on for an instance. State -&gt; (string) Indicates whether detailed monitoring is turned on. Otherwise, basic monitoring is turned on. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsEc2NetworkInterface -&gt; (structure) Details for an EC2 network interface. Attachment -&gt; (structure) The network interface attachment. AttachTime -&gt; (string) Indicates when the attachment initiated. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Secu- rity Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AttachmentId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the network interface at- tachment Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DeleteOnTermination -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether the network interface is deleted when the instance is terminated. DeviceIndex -&gt; (integer) The device index of the network interface attachment on the instance. InstanceId -&gt; (string) The ID of the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* InstanceOwnerId -&gt; (string) The Amazon Web Services account ID of the owner of the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Status -&gt; (string) The attachment state. Valid values: attaching | attached | de- taching | detached Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* NetworkInterfaceId -&gt; (string) The ID of the network interface. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SecurityGroups -&gt; (list) Security groups for the network interface. (structure) A security group associated