es details about a route table. A route ta- ble contains a set of rules, called routes, that determine where to direct network traffic from your subnet or gateway. AssociationSet -&gt; (list) The associations between a route table and one or more subnets or a gateway. (structure) The associations between a route table and one or more subnets or a gateway. AssociationState -&gt; (structure) The state of the association between a route table and a subnet or gateway. State -&gt; (string) The state of the association. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* StatusMessage -&gt; (string) The status message, if applicable. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* GatewayId -&gt; (string) The ID of the internet gateway or vir- tual private gateway. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Main -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether this is the main route table. RouteTableAssociationId -&gt; (string) The ID of the association. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RouteTableId -&gt; (string) The ID of the route table. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SubnetId -&gt; (string) The ID of the subnet. A subnet ID is not returned for an implicit association. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* OwnerId -&gt; (string) The ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the route table. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PropagatingVgwSet -&gt; (list) Describes a virtual private gateway propagating route. (structure) Describes a virtual private gateway propa- gating route. GatewayId -&gt; (string) The ID of the virtual private gateway. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RouteTableId -&gt; (string) The ID of the route table. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RouteSet -&gt; (list) The routes in the route table. (structure) Provides details about the routes in the route table. CarrierGatewayId -&gt; (string) The ID of the carrier gateway. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CoreNetworkArn -&gt; (string) The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the core network. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DestinationCidrBlock -&gt; (string) The IPv4 CIDR block used for t