ing) Indicates when the volume was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DeviceName -&gt; (string) The device name for the volume that is attached to the instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Encrypted -&gt; (boolean) Specifies whether the volume is encrypted. Size -&gt; (integer) The size of the volume, in GiBs. SnapshotId -&gt; (string) The snapshot from which the volume was created. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Status -&gt; (string) The volume state. Valid values are as follows: o available o creating o deleted o deleting o error o in-use Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KmsKeyId -&gt; (string) The ARN of the KMS key that was used to protect the volume encryption key for the volume. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Attachments -&gt; (list) The volume attachments. (structure) An attachment to an Amazon EC2 volume. AttachTime -&gt; (string) The datetime when the attachment initi- ated. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DeleteOnTermination -&gt; (boolean) Whether the EBS volume is deleted when the EC2 instance is terminated. InstanceId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the EC2 instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Status -&gt; (string) The attachment state of the volume. Valid values are as follows: o attaching o attached o busy o detaching o detached Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VolumeId -&gt; (string) The ID of the volume. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VolumeType -&gt; (string) The volume type. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VolumeScanStatus -&gt; (string) Indicates whether the volume was scanned or skipped. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsEc2Vpc -&gt; (structure) Details for an Amazon EC2 VPC. CidrBlockAssociationSet -&gt; (list) Information about the IPv4 CIDR blocks associ- ated with the VPC. (structure) An IPv4 CIDR block association. AssociationId -&gt; (string) The association ID for the IPv4 CIDR block. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CidrBlock -&gt; (string) The IPv4 CIDR block. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CidrBlockState -&gt; (string) Information about the state of the IPv4 CIDR block. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Ipv6CidrBlockAssociationSet -&gt; (list) Information about the IPv6 CIDR blocks associ- ated with the VPC. (structure) An IPV6 CIDR block association. AssociationId -&gt; (string) The association ID for the IPv6 CIDR block. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Ipv6CidrBlock -&gt; (string) The IPv6 CIDR block. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CidrBlockState -&gt; (string) Information about the state of the CIDR block. Valid values are as follows: o associating o associated o disassociating o disassociated o failed o failing Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DhcpOptionsId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the set of Dynamic Host Con- figuration Protocol (DHCP) options that are as- sociated with the VPC. If the default options are associated with the VPC, then this is de- fault. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* State -&gt; (string) The current state of the VPC. Valid values are available or pending . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsEc2Eip -&gt; (structure) Details about an Elastic IP address. InstanceId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the EC2 instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PublicIp -&gt; (string) A public IP address that is associated with the EC2 instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AllocationId -&gt; (string) The identifier that Amazon Web Services assigns to represent the allocation of the Elastic IP address for use with Amazon VPC. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AssociationId -&gt; (string) The identifier that represents the association of the Elastic IP address with an EC2 instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Domain -&gt; (string) The domain in which to allocate the address. If the address is for use with EC2 instances in a VPC, then Domain is vpc . Otherwise, Domain is standard . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PublicIpv4Pool -&gt; (string) The identifier of an IP address 