red. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LastFailureTime -&gt; (string) The last time when logs failed to be deliv- ered. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Secu- rity Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LastSuccessfulDeliveryTime -&gt; (string) The last time that logs were delivered suc- cessfully. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Secu- rity Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LoggingEnabled -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether logging is enabled. S3KeyPrefix -&gt; (string) Provides the prefix applied to the log file names. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsElbLoadBalancer -&gt; (structure) Contains details about a Classic Load Balancer. AvailabilityZones -&gt; (list) The list of Availability Zones for the load balancer. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* BackendServerDescriptions -&gt; (list) Information about the configuration of the EC2 instances. (structure) Provides information about the configura- tion of an EC2 instance for the load bal- ancer. InstancePort -&gt; (integer) The port on which the EC2 instance is listening. PolicyNames -&gt; (list) The names of the policies that are en- abled for the EC2 instance. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CanonicalHostedZoneName -&gt; (string) The name of the Amazon Route 53 hosted zone for the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CanonicalHostedZoneNameID -&gt; (string) The ID of the Amazon Route 53 hosted zone for the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreatedTime -&gt; (string) Indicates when the load balancer was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DnsName -&gt; (string) The DNS name of the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* HealthCheck -&gt; (structure) Information about the health checks that are conducted on the load balancer. HealthyThreshold -&gt; (integer) The number of consecutive health check suc- cesses required before the instance is moved to the Healthy state. Interval -&gt; (integer) The approximate interval, in seconds, be- tween health checks of an individual in- stance. Target -&gt; (string) The instance that is being checked. The target specifies the protocol and port. The available protocols are TCP, SSL, HTTP, and HTTPS. The range of valid ports is 1 through 65535. For the HTTP and HTTPS protocols, the tar- get also specifies the ping path. For the TCP protocol, the target is speci- fied as `` TCP: &lt;port&gt; `` . System Message: WARNING/2 (&lt;string&gt;:, line 19225) Inline literal start-string without end-string. For the SSL protocol, the target is specified as `` SSL.*&lt;port&gt;* `` . System Message: WARNING/2 (&lt;string&gt;:, line 19229) Inline literal start-string without end-string. For the HTTP and HTTPS protocols, the target is specified as `` &lt;pro- tocol&gt; :&lt;port&gt; /&lt;path to ping&gt; `` . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Timeout -&gt; (integer) The amount of time, in seconds, during which no response means a failed health check. UnhealthyThreshold -&gt; (integer) The number of consecutive health check failures that must occur before the in- stance is moved to the Unhealthy state. Instances -&gt; (list) List of EC2 instances for the load balancer. (structure) Provides information about an EC2 instance for a load balancer. InstanceId -&gt; (string) The instance identifier. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* ListenerDescriptions -&gt; (list) The policies that are enabled for the load bal- ancer listeners. (structure) Lists the policies that are enabled for a load balancer listener. Listener -&gt; (structure) Information about the listener. InstancePort -&gt; (integer) The port on which the instance is listening. InstanceProtocol -&gt; (string) The protocol to use to route traffic to instances. Valid values: HTTP | HTTPS | TCP | SSL Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LoadBalancerPort -&gt; (integer) The port on which the load balancer is listening. On EC2-VPC, you can specify any port from the range 1-65535. On EC2-Classic, you can specify any port from the following list: 25, 80, 443, 465, 587, 1024-65535. Protocol -&gt; (string) The load balancer transport protocol to use for routing. Valid values: HTTP | HTTPS | TCP | SSL Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SslCertificateId -&gt; (string) The ARN of the server certificate. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PolicyNames -&gt; (list) The policies enabled for the listener. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LoadBalancerAttributes -&gt; (structure) The attributes for a load balancer. AccessLog -&gt; (structure) Information about the access log configura- tion for the load balancer. If the access log is enabled, the load bal- ancer captures detailed information about all requests. It delivers the information to a specified S3 bucket. EmitInterval -&gt; (integer) The interval in minutes for publishing the access logs. You can publish access logs either every 5 minutes or every 60 minutes. Enabled -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether access logs are en- abled for the load balancer. S3BucketName -&gt; (string) The name of the S3 bucket where the ac- cess logs are stored. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* S3BucketPrefix -&gt; (string) The logical hierarchy that was created for the S3 bucket. If a prefix is not provided, the log is placed at the root level of the bucket. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* ConnectionDraining -&gt; (structure) Information about the connection draining configuration for the load balancer. If connection draining is enabled, the load balancer allows existing requests to com- plete before it shifts traffic away from a deregistered or unhealthy instance. Enabled -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether connection draining is enabled for the load balancer. Timeout -&gt; (integer) The maximum time, in seconds, to keep the existing connections open before deregistering the instances. ConnectionSettings -&gt; (structure) Connection settings for the load balancer. If an idle timeout is configured, the load balancer allows connections to remain idle for the specified duration. When a connec- tion is idle, no data is sent over the con- nection. IdleTimeout -&gt; (integer) The time, in seconds, that the connec- tion can be idle (no data is sent over the connection) before it is closed by the load balancer. CrossZoneLoadBalancing -&gt; (structure) Cross-zone load balancing settings for the load balancer. If cross-zone load balancing is enabled, the load balancer routes the request traf- fic evenly across all instances regardless of the Availability Zones. Enabled -&gt; (boolean) Indicates whether cross-zone load bal- ancing is enabled for the load balancer. AdditionalAttributes -&gt; (list) Any additional attributes for a load bal- ancer. (structure) Provides information about additional attributes for the load balancer. Key -&gt; (string) The name of the attribute. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Value -&gt; (string) The value of the attribute. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LoadBalancerName -&gt; (string) The name of the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Policies -&gt; (structure) The policies for a load balancer. AppCookieStickinessPolicies -&gt; (list) The stickiness policies that are created using CreateAppCookieStickinessPolicy . (structure) Contains information about a stickiness policy that was created using CreateApp- CookieStickinessPolicy . CookieName -&gt; (string) The name of the application cookie used for stickiness. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PolicyName -&gt; (string) The mnemonic name for the policy be- ing created. The name must be unique within the set of policies for the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LbCookieStickinessPolicies -&gt; (list) The stickiness policies that are created using CreateLBCookieStickinessPolicy . (structure) Contains information about a stickiness policy that was created using CreateLB- CookieStickinessPolicy . CookieExpirationPeriod -&gt; (long) The amount of time, in seconds, af- ter which the cookie is considered stale. If an expiration period is not specified, the stickiness ses- sion lasts for the duration of the browser session. PolicyName -&gt; (string) The name of the policy. The name must be unique within the set of policies for the load balancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* OtherPolicies -&gt; (list) The policies other than the stickiness policies. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Scheme -&gt; (string) The type of load balancer. Only provided if the load balancer is in a VPC. If Scheme is internet-facing , the load bal- ancer has a public DNS name that resolves to a public IP address. If Scheme is internal , the load balancer has a public DNS name that resolves to a private IP address. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SecurityGroups -&gt; (list) The security groups for the load balancer. Only provided if the load balancer is in a VPC. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SourceSecurityGroup -&gt; (structure) Information about the security group for the load balancer. This is the security group that is used for inbound rules. GroupName -&gt; (string) The name of the security group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* OwnerAlias -&gt; (string) The owner of the security group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Subnets -&gt; (list) The list of subnet identifiers for the load balancer. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VpcId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the VPC for the load bal- ancer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsIamGroup -&gt; (structure) Contains details about an IAM group. AttachedManagedPolicies -&gt; (list) A list of the managed policies that are at- tached to the IAM group. (structure) A managed policy that is attached to an IAM principal. PolicyName -&gt; (string) The name of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PolicyArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreateDate -&gt; (string) Indicates when the IAM group was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* GroupId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the IAM group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* GroupName -&gt; (string) The name of the IAM group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* GroupPolicyList -&gt; (list) The list of inline policies that are embedded in the group. (structure) A managed policy that is attached to the IAM group. PolicyName -&gt; (string) The name of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Path -&gt; (string) The path to the group. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsIamRole -&gt; (structure) Details about an IAM role. AssumeRolePolicyDocument -&gt; (string) The trust policy that grants permission to as- sume the role. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 131072 o pattern: [\u0009\u000A\u000D\u0020-\u007E\u00A1-\u00FF]+ AttachedManagedPolicies -&gt; (list) The list of the managed policies that are at- tached to the role. (structure) A managed policy that is attached to an IAM principal. PolicyName -&gt; (string) The name of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PolicyArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreateDate -&gt; (string) Indicates when the role was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* InstanceProfileList -&gt; (list) The list of instance profiles that contain this role. (structure) Information about an instance profile. Arn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the instance profile. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreateDate -&gt; (string) Indicates when the instance profile was created. For more information about the valida- tion and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* InstanceProfileId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the instance profile. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* InstanceProfileName -&gt; (string) The name of the instance profile. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Path -&gt; (string) The path to the instance profile. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Roles -&gt; (list) The roles associated with the instance profile. (structure) Information about a role associated with an instance profile. Arn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AssumeRolePolicyDocument -&gt; (string) The policy that grants an entity permission to assume the role. Constraints: o min: 1 o max: 131072 o pattern: [\u0009\u000A\u000D\u0020-\u007E\u00A1-\u00FF]+ CreateDate -&gt; (string) Indicates when the role was cre- ated. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Path -&gt; (string) The path to the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RoleId -&gt; (string) The identifier of the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RoleName -&gt; (string) The name of the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PermissionsBoundary -&gt; (structure) Information about the policy used to set the permissions boundary for an IAM principal. PermissionsBoundaryArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the policy used to set the per- missions boundary. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PermissionsBoundaryType -&gt; (string) The usage type for the permissions bound- ary. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RoleId -&gt; (string) The stable and unique string identifying the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RoleName -&gt; (string) The friendly name that identifies the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* RolePolicyList -&gt; (list) The list of inline policies that are embedded in the role. (structure) An inline policy that is embedded in the role. PolicyName -&gt; (string) The name of the policy. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* MaxSessionDuration -&gt; (integer) The maximum session duration (in seconds) that you want to set for the specified role. Path -&gt; (string) The path to the role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsKmsKey -&gt; (structure) Details about an KMS key. AWSAccountId -&gt; (string) The twelve-digit account ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the KMS key. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreationDate -&gt; (double) Indicates when the KMS key was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . KeyId -&gt; (string) The globally unique identifier for the KMS key. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KeyManager -&gt; (string) The manager of the KMS key. KMS keys in your Amazon Web Services account are either customer managed or Amazon Web Services managed. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KeyState -&gt; (string) The state of the KMS key. Valid values are as follows: o Disabled o Enabled o PendingDeletion o PendingImport o Unavailable Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Origin -&gt; (string) The source of the KMS key material. When this value is AWS_KMS , KMS created the key material. When this value is EXTERNAL , the key material was imported from your existing key management infrastructure or the KMS key lacks key mater- ial. When this value is AWS_CLOUDHSM , the key mate- rial was created in the CloudHSM cluster asso- ciated with a custom key store. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Description -&gt; (string) A description of the KMS key. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KeyRotationStatus -&gt; (boolean) Whether the key has key rotation enabled. AwsLambdaFunction -&gt; (structure) Details about a Lambda function. Code -&gt; (structure) An AwsLambdaFunctionCode object. S3Bucket -&gt; (string) An Amazon S3 bucket in the same Amazon Web Services Region as your function. The bucket can be in a different Amazon Web Services account. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* S3Key -&gt; (string) The Amazon S3 key of the deployment pack- age. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* S3ObjectVersion -&gt; (string) For versioned objects, the version of the deployment package object to use. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* ZipFile -&gt; (string) The base64-encoded contents of the deploy- ment package. Amazon Web Services SDK and Amazon Web Services CLI clients handle the encoding for you. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CodeSha256 -&gt; (string) The SHA256 hash of the function's deployment package. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DeadLetterConfig -&gt; (structure) The function's dead letter queue. TargetArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of an SQS queue or SNS topic. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Environment -&gt; (structure) The function's environment variables. Variables -&gt; (map) Environment variable key-value pairs. key -&gt; (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* value -&gt; (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Error -&gt; (structure) An AwsLambdaFunctionEnvironmentError ob- ject. ErrorCode -&gt; (string) The error code. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Message -&gt; (string) The error message. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* FunctionName -&gt; (string) The name of the function. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Handler -&gt; (string) The function that Lambda calls to begin execut- ing your function. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* KmsKeyArn -&gt; (string) The KMS key that is used to encrypt the func- tion's environment variables. This key is only returned if you've configured a customer man- aged customer managed key. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* LastModified -&gt; (string) Indicates when the function was last updated. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Layers -&gt; (list) The function's layers. (structure) An Lambda layer. Arn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the function layer. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CodeSize -&gt; (integer) The size of the layer archive in bytes. MasterArn -&gt; (string) For Lambda@Edge functions, the ARN of the mas- ter function. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* MemorySize -&gt; (integer) The memory that is allocated to the function. RevisionId -&gt; (string) The latest updated revision of the function or alias. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Role -&gt; (string) The function's execution role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Runtime -&gt; (string) The runtime environment for the Lambda func- tion. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Timeout -&gt; (integer) The amount of time that Lambda allows a func- tion to run before stopping it. TracingConfig -&gt; (structure) The function's X-Ray tracing configuration. Mode -&gt; (string) The tracing mode. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VpcConfig -&gt; (structure) The function's networking configuration. SecurityGroupIds -&gt; (list) A list of VPC security groups IDs. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* SubnetIds -&gt; (list) A list of VPC subnet IDs. (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* VpcId -&gt; (string) The ID of the VPC. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Version -&gt; (string) The version of the Lambda function. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Architectures -&gt; (list) The instruction set architecture that the func- tion uses. Valid values are x86_64 or arm64 . (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* PackageType -&gt; (string) The type of deployment package that's used to deploy the function code to Lambda. Set to Im- age for a container image and Zip for a .zip file archive. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsLambdaLayerVersion -&gt; (structure) Details for a Lambda layer version. Version -&gt; (long) The version number. CompatibleRuntimes -&gt; (list) The layer's compatible function runtimes . The following list includes deprecated run- times. For more information, see Runtime depre- cation policy in the Lambda Developer Guide . Array Members: Maximum number of 5 items. Valid Values: nodejs | nodejs4.3 | nodejs6.10 | nodejs8.10 | nodejs10.x | nodejs12.x | nodejs14.x | nodejs16.x | java8 | java8.al2 | java11 | python2.7 | python3.6 | python3.7 | python3.8 | python3.9 | dotnetcore1.0 | dotnet- core2.0 | dotnetcore2.1 | dotnetcore3.1 | dot- net6 | nodejs4.3-edge | go1.x | ruby2.5 | ruby2.7 | provided | provided.al2 | nodejs18.x | python3.10 | java17 | ruby3.2 | python3.11 | nodejs20.x | provided.al2023 | python3.12 | java21 (string) Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CreatedDate -&gt; (string) Indicates when the version was created. For more information about the validation and formatting of timestamp fields in Security Hub CSPM, see Timestamps . Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* AwsRdsDbInstance -&gt; (structure) Details about an Amazon RDS database instance. AssociatedRoles -&gt; (list) The IAM roles associated with the DB instance. (structure) An IAM role associated with the DB in- stance. RoleArn -&gt; (string) The ARN of the IAM role that is associ- ated with the DB instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* FeatureName -&gt; (string) The name of the feature associated with the IAM role. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* Status -&gt; (string) Describes the state of the association between the IAM role and the DB in- stance. The Status property returns one of the following values: o ACTIVE - The IAM role ARN is associ- ated with the DB instance and can be used to access other Amazon Web Ser- vices services on your behalf. o PENDING - The IAM role ARN is being associated with the DB instance. o INVALID - The IAM role ARN is associ- ated with the DB instance. But the DB instance is unable to assume the IAM role in order to access other Amazon Web Services services on your behalf. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* CACertificateIdentifier -&gt; (string) The identifier of the CA certificate for this DB instance. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DBClusterIdentifier -&gt; (string) If the DB instance is a member of a DB cluster, contains the name of the DB cluster that the DB instance is a member of. Constraints: o pattern: .*\S.* DBInstanceIdentifier -&gt; (string) Contains a user-supplied database identifier. This identifier is the unique key that identi- fies a DB instance. Constraints: o pattern